    "note": [
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "The City of Palo Alto has detailed in its Sustainability and Climate Action Plan (S/CAP)\r\nits strategy to reach an 80% reduction of greenhouse gas emissions by 2030, relative to 1990\r\nlevels. This comprehensive work is emblematic of the pioneering work that the City of Palo Alto\r\nis doing to be a leader in progress towards a carbon neutral future. In 2018, California Governor\r\nJerry Brown signed Executive Order B-55-18 that sets a statewide target of reaching carbon\r\nneutrality by 2045. For the Winter Quarter Public Policy Practicum Project, the City has asked\r\nour team to evaluate the potential of Negative Emissions Technologies (NETs) and Palo Alto’s\r\nUrban Forest as strategies to capture the remaining 20% of emissions, or 156,024 metric tons of\r\nCO2 post 80x30, needed to reach carbon neutrality by the state’s target. Through the course of\r\nour research, we identified best practices in other governments, conducted stakeholder\r\ninterviews, evaluated the state of the NET industry, and estimated the sequestration potential of\r\nimprovements made to the Urban Forest and other natural sequestration opportunities.",
            "type": "abstract",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        },
        {
            "structuredValue": [],
            "parallelValue": [],
            "groupedValue": [],
            "value": "Doty, L., Jacquez, M., Mahale, N., Odunowo, T., and Paladino, B. (2022). Evaluating Strategies and Scenarios for Carbon Neutrality for the City of Palo Alto. Stanford Digital Repository. Available at https://purl.stanford.edu/wz019qn1037",
            "type": "preferred citation",
            "identifier": [],
            "note": [],
            "appliesTo": []
        }
    ],
